From eabb3501baec3a5bf87942e53ea1a3c3202cda4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:58:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(aux): Gemini cancel-mid-stream closes on the
 reading worker once, and its sockets get shut down

Follow-ups from the exact-head review of PR #2148 (card t_01a1d4b61dcb2670).

1. Test: AsyncGeminiNativeClient runs the create and every _async_stream step through
   aux_provider_handoff.run_in_thread, but nothing covered it. The new real-TLS test in
   test_aux_stranger_close_siblings.py streams one chunk, then cancels while the second step's worker is
   blocked on the stalled body. It pins: the SQLite header survives fd reuse, the client is closed once, on
   that step's worker (never the loop thread), and the scope's socket sweep reached the socket.

2. _close_pair: AsyncGeminiNativeClient wraps the sync leaf itself, and its close() is a coroutine. On an
   abandoned to_thread worker (no running loop) _schedule_async_close ran asyncio.run, whose to_thread closed
   the leaf on yet another executor thread, and then the leaf was closed again directly. FD-safe (fn had
   returned) but roundabout. Skip the async wrapper's close when its _real_client is the sync leaf being
   closed next. RED before: closed_on == ['asyncio_0', 'asyncio_1'].

3. _iter_pool_sockets also walks a client's `_http` (GeminiNativeClient's httpx client). Before, the
   abandoned-Gemini sweep logged tcp_shutdown=0: the fd stayed safe, but the provider read (read timeout
   1200 s) kept running, and billing, after a cancel. RED before: tcp_shutdown=0.

4. run_in_thread docstring: force_close_tcp_sockets cannot reach Bedrock's boto3/urllib3 sockets, so a
   cancelled Bedrock worker gets tcp_shutdown=0; the fd stays safe but the read and billing run to its own
   timeout. The sync twin behaves the same way. The siblings test docstring now lists Gemini.

Tests: tests/agent/test_aux_stranger_close_siblings.py + test_aux_abandoned_provider_tls_fd.py green;
every test file importing the touched modules (41 files, 657 tests) green.
